//! The `border-inline-color` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property
//! defines the color of the logical inline borders of an element, which maps to a physical border
//! color depending on the element's writing mode, directionality, and text orientation. It
//! corresponds to the `border-top-color` and `border-bottom-color`, or `border-right-color` and
//! `border-left-color` property depending on the values defined for `writing-mode`, `direction`, and
//! `text-orientation`.
//!
//! Initial: border-inline-start-color: currentcolor; border-inline-end-color: currentcolor.
//! Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: <'border-top-color'>{1,2}
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-borders-4/#propdef-border-inline-color
//!
//! Author guide:
//! https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/border-inline-color
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

